{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_059a883de673835b4c954621f5e5b33618215d2cfcb75ee46ef518fe64ab7c1e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8cac1cf458a5126b7e31d4977313c27d0d2ec50e13149177c77c5db5480b2c47"],"source_ids":["src_587abd3e0a195643a6772252f3cf2216"],"text":"Repository development practice: the documented development flow is to create a branch, implement and test, run format and type checks, open a PR with an English title and description, and request review once CI passes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0d11f6f74da7bbbb3995bc56eb90c6fd330d5f0e18fcbca9d4e6b3083d48f098","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3534f58443f1895cde83ebeeb32d351bd674435bff16f0f44dbe35680a8d29bc","slc_4313f1e1e4e3e99fc5bb2970dd861ff782415f37c0480ceb20f1664d40159fae","slc_4cc4381e1dca49d7d76a5328e693a2cd847caab72d4c05950b1940452cd8b28c","slc_4d4b3295d63ef03a41b47ce1abfade668b9b3374b16ba9ddae728feb0354983f","slc_e2ada9c57a140ceb04a759d67d8728e06ca975c4e1272ea1b71c83a1ebcf0206"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"Users can interact with the deployed system through a web dashboard, a Slack bot, RESTful API endpoints, and a GitHub Actions integration that triggers agents from repository events.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0e1c3fd2490d7b7f9b21159e405c2b0b861730f73d4b947691a9c09483e7954c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4978bbdedb046946c483abc64de1dc854302e8aef3c4dbb3da810e306f7d8a04"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"When using the GitHub App option, the system is limited to repositories under a single organization (app installation), per the README note.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1187204a34b2752d027d42963473c6aad209cd06f58e637817e6bd13ae48cb2d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5984e01492086e18eb4de48f044a6473814d51772d17693db9984dfbe8052937","slc_75f4ab191befa989c1adaf54a46b39766488c5b73c13d821e7ac4520cfe5978f","slc_852c626ef55273c3637664292a85e45a1964a38ecf10f7c08078399dd9a08a7a","slc_fc376aaa6fb106f35cfb5e82becfa4df4238a125767b1c407266a07f9d0fb7ab"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"Slack messages reach an API Gateway webhook feeding a Lambda, which publishes to AppSync Events and stores history in DynamoDB; a Worker Manager provisions an EC2 instance plus EBS volume per new thread, and workers subscribe back to AppSync for messages.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1b1c8cf5102e89e305faebae96ead27abcf0c9b42dc579aa890159cf5be85c1a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a6b3f51237749897e054e8e13f9231930adc7658073242e6316f6c723ed681d","slc_abe950589472188beb09beeaf96e048f658c28ebe6a89d041cad6ea99d50637a"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"The agent acts as an MCP client; integrations are configured by editing packages/worker/mcp.json and redeploying, after which new agents can use MCP servers as tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_41240c5e4120c4c4e8c5078975b471e78af5d15ebf26684fabd62c7012d1cff9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_995aad854948117b6f14c316a3e63acd711b2b3cd61c59e8f0bf4ec33db27128"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"Deployment prerequisites are Node.js 22+, npm 9+, AWS CLI, an IAM profile with appropriate permissions, and Docker.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5dfc841670e55ddaea8032482e841f71b1ffd9decfb4ea06fdfd1fc576feef3f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_41fac397a4046a8b8384af28b6f1b16865ab1650712599ce106ce18ef213529d"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"Access controls differ by channel: Slack access can be restricted via SLACK_ADMIN_USER_ID_LIST, Cognito self-sign-up is disabled by default with equal permissions for account holders, REST API access requires knowing an API key, and any repository collaborator can invoke the GitHub Action.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7d2d0760ad6e7d0b6301cb3a6433c73114196785334155cc0e2ca987ac87bcf9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_27fc70a3887876c90cfb80adf8872b5f0c0b510cbf6bc614fca7b596665daf74","slc_d097e8cb12f4980a83fa423ef034e69947977afc7623330bb2046978f8f3f55b"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"The agent runs on AWS Bedrock models; the cost table assumes Claude Sonnet 3.7 usage, and a web UI setting selects the default foundation model for new sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9d3cb2c3b9a0aba78b66e321ba26a93bbd4b4ea2274dbbd31dc98179c7c3114a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2cebd920b37cd794f86805113e4588e8f0cfe17c029cf4fca5bd2c059ce02013","slc_b2c7aa581e7aca03a25171a0d2e1233d8a8d37ccfee485050d9ce12f9f1393ae","slc_b8ec0560bf6a6e203980c7fae4722a05bf1177c71bba913f85a77f07b55a851f"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"Worker instances receive minimal IAM policies by default (logging, self-termination, S3 read), and extra permissions can be attached via the WORKER_ADDITIONAL_POLICIES environment variable.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a1abfdd25798982ab7a7f23dae9e1f4cf2a7244df937ddb2e885023e1676fdac","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4978bbdedb046946c483abc64de1dc854302e8aef3c4dbb3da810e306f7d8a04","slc_53d5c8e2860a903d4fb05a171ce5bc18652cda181edd1eac85aa24310923afe2"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"GitHub integration supports either a personal access token stored in SSM (simpler, single-user) or a GitHub App (recommended for teams), and with the App option only repositories under a single organization installation can be used.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.5,"id":"clm_b4d655ac512d332f1d365933375bdb1439a9e3d25ee1baf5ee628523d42c18f5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=inference; facet=evaluation","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_504373405e1b14b6009ec374d93a4ef74dae683f4720a1ec70d78f06c4f73363","slc_e4f11175a042eb7ae1100da8e55b9ee7dfff0ab438d09ee86b21bcc28d839f91","slc_f84ac9c1896866943fddfcb8312b4f224b6bf0c111c75b11fe719e8a1b36b405"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"The README showcases example agent sessions and a search link to public pull requests authored by the agent, suggesting demonstration-based evidence of capability rather than a formal benchmark harness.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c5717364b48e2045cecc46b1d3487ed184b7bd097f5b53dea33c5569e1cd71c7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"aws-samples/remote-swe-agents@3a34a9b4d0da snapshot a5513177dfea5d49","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_05dd82b58419e15620db049ec3c62bde60a9ef7d1c29d4b16944781b7cba9b33","slc_40e4d9fd70bc43a67354418b02e82508fcb27cd5e0bc89e4c9131319e530f425"],"source_ids":["src_13e91e8555f05c699f77d1e8ce2b7c6b"],"text":"The system is designed as a single-tenant deployment, one per tenant, relying on a pay-as-you-go model so multiple deployments carry minimal infrastructure overhead.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_7ca510f7e3ec4340959fa207a7ca7a5b"}
